{"ts": "2026-10-26T14:49:58.315544Z", "run_id": "r-20261026T1445Z-e448", "unit": "openspec:audit-chain-verifiable", "seq": 26, "type": "delegate.result", "question": "Q-003", "id": "Q-003", "status": "answered", "reason": "The question comes from design.md's open questions and asks who runs the job and with which environment. The MVP design (section 15) answers the operational question: external cron/K8s CronJob, ad hoc by an operator under compose. The unit's own design (D6) and proposal (Impact) fix the environment for this change: DATABASE_URL and mintkey_models importable via PYTHONPATH, no sys.path change in production code, and no deployment artefact listed in the impact. I confirmed in the repository that no Dockerfile or compose entry exists for the job (Glob of Dockerfiles and grep of compose/workflow files), and that the blocked tasks test the job without any deployment (fake session, importlib load of main.py). So the tasks are not blocked and the documents settle the scope; no business decision remains for this unit.", "called": true, "tasks": ["1.1", "2.1", "2.2"], "target": null, "kind": "ambiguous", "profile": "delegate-fable", "model": "claude-fable-5-1", "cli": "claude-code", "cost_usd": 1.17977775, "decision": "answer", "answer_sha256": "b3ae880bf2ad8147c706c5ce6383b0d6eeb94a5adea8c7a16dcd9a8e9b547c31", "checked": [{"ref": ".kiro/specs/mintkey-mvp/design.md:1053", "quote": "A small Python script `audit-verify-job/` packaged as a one‑shot container, scheduled by an external cron / Kubernetes CronJob (in compose: ad‑hoc invocation by an operator via the on‑demand endpoint).", "claim": "The project's MVP design states who runs the verify job and how: an external scheduler, or an operator ad hoc under compose."}, {"ref": "apps/audit-verify-job/main.py:12", "quote": "DATABASE_URL  — asyncpg-compatible DSN (e.g. postgresql+asyncpg://...)", "claim": "The job's documented environment today is a DATABASE_URL with an asyncpg DSN."}, {"ref": "spec:design.md#decisions", "quote": "The job imports `mintkey_models`, so it\nruns where that package and its dependencies (SQLAlchemy, pydantic) are importable, e.g.\n`PYTHONPATH=packages/python/mintkey-models python apps/audit-verify-job/main.py`. No `sys.path` change in production\ncode.", "claim": "The unit's design fixes the job's run environment after the change and forbids a sys.path change in production code."}, {"ref": "spec:proposal.md#impact", "quote": "The verify job now imports `mintkey_models`: run it where that package is importable,\n  e.g. `PYTHONPATH=packages/python/mintkey-models python apps/audit-verify-job/main.py` with the job's existing\n  `DATABASE_URL`.", "claim": "The proposal tells operators how to run the job and lists no Dockerfile, compose service or chart job in its impact, so adding one is outside scope."}, {"ref": "openspec/changes/audit-chain-verifiable/tasks.md:44", "quote": "import `verify` by that name (`main.py` imports it so), and load `<repo>/apps/audit-verify-job/main.py` with\n  `importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(\"audit_verify_job_main\", ...)`.", "claim": "Task 2.1 tests the job by loading main.py directly with sys.path set in the test, so no deployment definition is needed for the blocked tasks."}, {"ref": "apps/admin-api/src/admin_api/api/audit_admin.py:11", "quote": "import from audit-verify-job, which is a separate deployment unit.", "claim": "The code already treats the job as a separate deployment unit from admin-api, consistent with the MVP design's external scheduling."}]}
